0|0@DebateAChristian^1440424259#cudvdah:heyvina$:Well, I started from an understanding that most Christians do not live as their God calls, they get confused with dogma and taking things literally to suit their own selfish motives or confirm what people they trust told them at an early age or vulnerable time. I didn't see the power and transformation they claim existed. So I stepped back and worked to eradicate all manufactured guilt of religion and addiction to some higher power who tells us how to live and we call out to and doesn't answer and live on my own idea of what I wanted life to be. Over time I continued to feel like I was missing some little connection to life. Some would say that was a result of being indoctrinated early, and that may have made me more open to it, but I worked tirelessly to rid myself of all presuppositions and see things objectively. I worked on forgiveness for Christians who clearly do not understand the way people nor the world works and give false hope to people who end up feeling confused and tricked. I started from the basis that people will believe just about anything to feel safer, powerful, comforted, controlling. Then I looked at the patterns between religions and philosophies. Took all the similarities, and applied them. At their core, they are all saying certain things. So I decided to pretend those things were true. Wrote off anything more as just human construction. I've written a little paragraph on what I think is the first step in seeing a glimpse of the source of life, but most people write it off. Lemme know if you're interested in trying it and I'll send it to you. I don't know what God is called. I know what attributes are him. Love, selflessness, grace, peace, etc Some people would say that I just worship general good human things and apply meditation or habit forming to bring them into my life. But it's my experience that when one lives this way, they realize that just as people used to see weather as random, or anything really, we start to understand the system behind it. We only have just begun to understand the infinite intricacy of the brain and the power of transformation and creation possible inside it.
