2|0@DebateAChristian^1440345147#cucvq21:heyvina$:I rarely try to impose my ideas on other people, only when people I know are discussing their lives will I offer a conversation for both of our edification, and in response to posts on here, in case people are actually curious, they are after all asking about the subject. The perceptions for me are things that everyone, Christian, Muslim, atheist can perceive, I just personally am able to immerse myself in them more when I attribute them as a whole to a source and purpose. Today it's simply training myself to not give in to hopelessness in regards to my job, to step away and focus on all the good that has been done and will be done. In turn, I'm not disparaging employees and sucking their motivation, but am working on lifting myself up and in turn lifting everyone up around me. My mantra for today is 'head held high'. Too often I focus on all the bad, and it paralyzes me, I can't look people in the eyes, I lash out or am sarcastic or passive aggressive. Everyone should know that they are deep down good, shit can be piled on by mistakes or circumstance or people, but everyone has an innate good inside, I call it the source and we should celebrate this inside ourselves and work to habitually free our minds from the darkness that this world throws at us. I also am trying to sing a lot as I sit, as I walk. I think everyone should always be singing.
